Project: Maven + SonarQube – Java Code Quality Analysis Without Jenkins
Standalone DevOps Project
 No Jenkins / No CI/CD

1. Project overview
In this hands-on project, we will integrate Apache Maven with SonarQube to perform static code analysis on a Java application.

The main objective is to build a Java application using Maven and analyze its source code using SonarQube to identify bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells, security issues, and code-quality problems.

This is a standalone project. We will execute Maven commands manually from the terminal and send the analysis results to SonarQube.


Real-world use case
Imagine a Java development team working on an e-commerce application.

Developers write Java code and use Maven to build the application. Before the application is released, the team wants to check:
- Are there any bugs in the Java code?
- Are there any security vulnerabilities?
- Is the code duplicated?
- Are there unnecessary or poorly written methods?
- Does the code follow coding standards?
- Does the project meet the required quality standards?
SonarQube helps developers identify these problems before releasing the application.


